[17592186084113 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084113 #edb/ref 1061 20565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084113 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c7acf227-0405-52eb-b5a9-6874c264b053" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084113 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084114 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084114 #edb/ref 1061 20566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084114 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "55717602-2643-55f3-9ba3-f1359bfa5ed3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084114 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084115 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084115 #edb/ref 1061 20567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084115 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c5ef9564-d57a-578d-92b9-ae3aee5d0a39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084115 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084116 #edb/ref 1061 20568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084116 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "12763dad-dbd5-5f26-bc50-389926344c0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084116 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084446 #edb/ref 1064 "Given a collection of $n$ objects, there are $n!$ ways to arrange those objects in a sequence.\n\n- For example, suppose we have $n=2$ objects: $A$ and $B.$ Then there are $2!=2 \\cdot 1 = 2$ arrangements:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{A,B}_{1\\text{st way}}, \\quad \\underbrace{B,A}_{2\\text{nd way}}\n$$\n\n- Likewise, suppose we have $n=3$ objects: $A,$ $B,$ and $C.$ Then there are $3!=3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1 = 6$ arrangements:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{A,B,C}_{1\\text{st way}},\\quad\n\\underbrace{A,C,B}_{2\\text{nd way}}, \\quad \n\\underbrace{B,A,C}_{3\\text{rd way}}, \\quad \n\\underbrace{B,C,A}_{4\\text{th way}}, \\quad \n\\underbrace{C,A,B}_{5\\text{th way}},\\quad \n\\underbrace{C,B,A}_{6\\text{th way}}\n$$\n\nThis pattern extends to any number of objects." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084446 #edb/ref 1065 3680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084446 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0753e8b5-a022-5644-84fc-f43f1dcf6761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084446 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084447 #edb/ref 1064 "The mathematical name for an arrangement is a **permutation**. With a permutation, *the order matters*. This means that for the letters $A,B,C,D,E$, the permutation\n\n$$\nA,B,C,D,E\n$$\n\n    is different from\n\n$$\nE,D,C,B,A.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084447 #edb/ref 1065 3681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084447 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "29dee738-c115-51e6-b129-3ddb6d812d68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084447 #edb/ref 1067 "Permutations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284936 #edb/ref 1080 "48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284936 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284936 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "110abfe8-256f-586f-8c14-cdbacbf98aa0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285763 #edb/ref 1080 "24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285763 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285763 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6a8cbe92-7d56-57d4-ac77-8dcc36070b12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285871 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285871 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285871 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "75559a19-2283-512d-bed1-5bd115893a57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285933 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285933 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285933 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7c34d0e6-2814-5d2f-be61-88b870668d34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286271 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286271 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286271 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a1f7b5bb-d5a9-5ca5-9642-1dbe2e08c1b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287239 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186